\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of polynomial hint preconditioning{}. (a) Standard patch transformer: each patch is embedded independently. (b) Our method adds a Chebyshev FIR-filtered hint channel (orange) that is concatenated with the target before the input projection. Only the input projection layer is wider; the transformer encoder and output projection are identical. The total overhead is 12K parameters (0.11\%).\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{4}{Overview of \method {}. (a) Standard patch transformer: each patch is embedded independently. (b) Our method adds a Chebyshev FIR-filtered hint channel (orange) that is concatenated with the target before the input projection. Only the input projection layer is wider; the transformer encoder and output projection are identical. The total overhead is 12K parameters (0.11\%).\relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
